Profiles:
=========
1. Spring boot profiles enables us to use different types of configurations in the different environments with out refactoring
the actual code.
2. It can be done by define different types application.properties files for different environment for example:
applcation-dev.properties.
appliction-qa.propeties. We can switch to different configuration for the same code base at run time

1. java -jar kiran.java --spring.profiles.active=dev,test,qa. here the dev,test,qa environmens are activated.
2. The latest environment will overrides the previous environments application.properties.

@Profile("dev") is used for the creation of the beans only in specific environment 

